6. APPLICATION NAVIGATION AND AUTHENTICATION FLOW

The application must follow this order:

Public Landing Page → Login or Registration → Role-Specific Dashboard → Selected Feature Page → Sign Out

Landing page

Anyone can access the landing page without logging in.

Public visitors can explore the product, browse permitted public alerts, learn how reporting works, and choose to register or sign in.

Authentication

After successful authentication:

Retrieve the authenticated user's profile and role.
Validate that the account is active.
Determine the user's authorized organization, if applicable.
Redirect to the correct dashboard.
Load only the navigation and data the user is permitted to access.
Protected routes

Unauthenticated users must not access protected pages.

If an unauthenticated visitor opens a protected URL, redirect them to login.

After login, return them to their originally requested page only if they are authorized to access it. Otherwise, redirect them to their role-specific dashboard.

Sign-out behavior

When a user signs out:

End the authenticated session through the configured authentication provider.
Clear sensitive client-side state and cached private data.
Prevent protected pages from remaining accessible through ordinary navigation.
Redirect to the public landing page.
Update the navigation to show public actions.
Do not display the previous user's dashboard or private information.
Do not silently sign the user back in unless an explicit supported authentication flow requires it.

Use secure session handling appropriate to the selected authentication provider.

Registration

Provide a public registration page for citizens.

Organization accounts and staff accounts must use a controlled onboarding process.

Do not allow anyone to select Platform Super Administrator from a public registration dropdown.

Organization administrators should invite or provision their staff through authorized workflows.

Validate email addresses, password requirements, required fields, duplicate accounts, and account status.

Provide password-reset functionality through the configured authentication provider.

