Examples:

A citizen may submit a new report.
An organization administrator may review the report.
An authorized administrator may assign work.
Assigned field staff may record progress.
Authorized staff may submit a resolution for verification.
An authorized administrator may approve or reject the proposed resolution.
A citizen may request review or reopening when permitted by policy.
Only authorized roles may perform final closure.

Validate each transition against:

Current report status.
Authenticated actor.
Actor role.
Organization membership.
Assignment relationship.
Required fields.
Relevant policy settings.

Every successful transition must create a history entry and the appropriate notifications.

Alert lifecycle

Support:

Draft → Scheduled → Published → Expired or Withdrawn

Validate publication and expiry rules.

Only authorized organization administrators may publish alerts for their organization.

The backend must verify permissions and record publication history.

Duplicate reports

Use deterministic matching suggestions based on configurable criteria such as:

Similar category.
Nearby coordinates.
Similar submission time.
Matching normalized address.
Similar title.

Do not automatically merge or discard reports without an authorized review process.

Assignment policy

Use configurable category-to-department mappings.

Allow authorized administrators to select eligible staff.

Do not automatically assign work to an arbitrary user.

Resolution verification

Require the appropriate work details and evidence based on configured policy.

Record verification outcomes and reasons.

Do not silently mark reports resolved simply because field staff clicked a button.

